Template: harmony-ap/reconfigure-notice
Type: note
Description: Reconfiguration notice
  Reconfiguration updates connection parameters and service settings.
  .
  Database: if you change connection parameters, ensure the target
  database is properly set up. The package will not create schemas
  or run migrations during reconfiguration.
  .
  Certificates: you will be given the option to rotate the security
  and TLS certificates independently. Rotating a certificate backs
  up the current keystore and generates a new key pair.

Template: harmony-ap/rotate_security_keystore
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Rotate the AP security certificate?
  The security certificate is used for AS4 message signing,
  encryption, and authentication between access points.
  This will back up the current security keystore and generate
  a new key pair. The truststore (partner certificates) is preserved.

Template: harmony-ap/rotate_tls_keystore
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Rotate the TLS certificate?
  This will back up the current TLS keystore and generate
  a new key pair and server certificate.

Template: harmony-ap/usedynamicdiscovery
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Enable SML/SMP dynamic discovery?
  Enables automatic endpoint discovery for AS4 messaging
  via the Service Metadata Locator (SML).

Template: harmony-ap/smlzone
Type: string
Description: SML zone for dynamic discovery
  The SML zone identifies the network used for dynamic partner
  discovery (e.g. edelivery.tech.ec.europa.eu).

Template: harmony-ap/adminuser
Type: string
Default: harmony
Description: Administrator username

Template: harmony-ap/adminpassword
Type: password
Description: Administrator initial password
  Leave blank to generate a random password.

Template: harmony-ap/serverdn
Type: string
Description: Server TLS certificate distinguished name
  Identifies this server in TLS connections.
  Format: CN=hostname (e.g. CN=ap.example.com)

Template: harmony-ap/serversan
Type: string
Description: Server TLS certificate subject alternative name
  Additional hostnames or IPs that clients use to verify the
  server identity.
  Format: DNS:hostname (e.g. DNS:ap.example.com)

Template: harmony-ap/securitydn
Type: string
Description: Security certificate distinguished name
  The security certificate is used for AS4 message signing
  and encryption between access points.
  Format: CN=name (e.g. CN=selfsigned)

Template: harmony-ap/partyname
Type: string
Default: selfsigned
Description: Party name
  Used as the certificate alias and AS4 party identifier.

Template: harmony-ap/tomcatport
Type: string
Default: 8443
Description: Web server HTTPS port

Template: harmony-ap/database-host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: Database host
  Use localhost for a database running on this machine.

Template: harmony-ap/database-type
Type: select
Choices: mysql, mariadb
Default: mysql
Description: Database server type
  Both MySQL 8.x and MariaDB 10.6+ are supported.

Template: harmony-ap/database-port
Type: string
Default: 3306
Description: Database port
  Must match database configuration.

Template: harmony-ap/database-schema
Type: string
Default: harmony_ap
Description: Database schema name
  When using a remote database, the schema must exist.

Template: harmony-ap/database-user
Type: string
Default: harmony_ap
Description: Database user name
  When using a remote database, the database user must exist
  and have rights to the "${db_schema}" database schema.

Template: harmony-ap/database-password
Type: password
Description: Database user password
  Leave blank to keep the existing password or to generate
  a random password during a fresh installation.
